is  determined to require archiving, rearranges the files so that
is empty, has the last period’s logs in it, has the next to  last
period’s  logs  in it and so on, up to a user‐specified number of
archived logs.  Optionally the archived logs can be compressed to
save space.  A log can be  archived  for  three  reasons:  It  is
larger  than  the  configured  size (in kilobytes).  A configured
number of hours have elapsed since the  log  was  last  archived.
The  configured  time for rotation of the log occurred within the
last 60 minutes.  The granularity of is dependent on how often it
is scheduled to run by It is recommended that be run once hourly.
